<title>UK: HORSE RACING-1991 NATIONAL WINNER SEAGRAM DIES.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-1991 NATIONAL WINNER SEAGRAM DIES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seagram, winner of the 1991 Aintree Grand National, died on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 17-year-old, trained by David Barons and owned by Sir Eric Parker, retired from racing three years ago after poor performances. He did not win a race after Aintree.</p>
</text>
